course: dictionary
lesson: 3614
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning is right. «A sandwich is made from 2 slices of bread with the filling in between.» Here the filling is the food that goes inside the sandwich.
explain: Now look at this one: «A filling repairs a hole in a tooth; the dentist numbs the area first.» The filling here is not food at all. It is the material a dentist puts into a hole in a tooth. The words tooth, dentist and numbs are the clues.
explain: Always check your meaning with the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word and read it aloud. If it still makes sense, you are probably right. If it sounds silly, look for another meaning.
fact: Filling is a noun when it means the food inside a pie, sandwich, cake or pastry.
fact: Filling is also the soft material inside cushions, pillows and toys, and the material a dentist puts into a hole in a tooth.
fact: Filling food makes you feel full quickly.
fact: Filling is the -ing form of «fill», which means putting something into a container until it is full.
exercise: «A sandwich is made from 2 slices of bread with the filling in between.» What is the filling? | The bread | The plate it is served on | *The food placed inside the sandwich | The knife used to cut it
exercise: «A filling repairs a hole in a tooth; the dentist numbs the area first.» What does filling mean here? | A type of sweet | *The material the dentist puts into a hole in a tooth | A kind of toothbrush | To eat something quickly
exercise: Which word describes food that makes you feel full quickly? | Cold | Hungry | *Filling | Light
test: A pillow has soft filling inside it. What does filling mean here? | Something to sleep on | A hole in the wall | The cover of the pillow | *The soft material inside the pillow
test: «A tank is filling at 5 litres a minute.» What is the tank doing? | Being painted a new colour | Cracking under pressure | Emptying out slowly | *Getting fuller with water, 5 litres each minute
exam: Which sentence uses filling as the -ing form of fill? | *Jake is filling the jug with cold water | The pillow is soft and full | Her tooth needed a filling | The filling was sweet and sticky
